# Simple admin.py

- Keep admin basic. Do not use `@admin.register` + big `ModelAdmin` classes.
- Use `admin.site.register(Model)`.
- No inlines, fieldsets, or filter_horizontal unless the user asks.

```python
# GOOD
from django.contrib import admin
from .models import Course, Enrollment, QuizQuestion

admin.site.register(Course)
admin.site.register(Enrollment)
admin.site.register(QuizQuestion)

# BAD
@admin.register(Course)
class CourseAdmin(admin.ModelAdmin):
    list_display = (...)
    inlines = [QuizQuestionInline]
```
